  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Exploring the Impact of Technology-Facilitated Gender-Based Violence in the Caribbean</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AI biases pose a significant risk of leaving women behind in all areas of economic, political, and social life. The biases embedded in AI systems can contribute to Technology-Facilitated Gender-Based Violence (TFGBV), which encompasses various forms. This initiative aims to explore the perceptions of discrimination by AI algorithms as well as the awareness of potential biases within AI affecting Caribbean women and girls and knowledge of AI&apos;s broader impacts on Caribbean society using culturally relevant approaches while aligning with the Gender Policy Action Area of UNESCO&#x2019;s Recommendation on the Ethics of AI (2021).</narrative>
  </description>
